---
// What acquire() does, and the states a pooled connection moves through.
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 400 330" width="100%" role="img" aria-labelledby="cp-lc-t cp-lc-d">
  <title id="cp-lc-t">Acquiring a connection, and a pooled connection's life</title>
  <desc id="cp-lc-d">
    Top: acquire checks three cases in order. If an idle connection is free, take it. If the pool is
    below its maximum, open a new one, which costs a few milliseconds. If the pool is at its maximum,
    wait in line, and fail with an error when the acquire timeout runs out.
    Bottom: a connection moves from idle to in use when acquired, and back to idle when released,
    after the pool rolls back any open transaction and resets session state. An idle connection is
    closed when it has been idle too long, reaches its maximum lifetime, or fails a health check.
    A connection that breaks while in use is closed instead of being returned.
  </desc>
  <defs>
    <marker id="cp-lc-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)" />
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <text x="4" y="20" font-size="18" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">acquire(), in order</text>
  <rect x="4" y="32" width="392" height="30" rx="5" stroke-width="1.5" style="fill: var(--viz-ok-soft); stroke: var(--viz-ok)" />
  <text x="14" y="53" font-size="16" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">1. an idle one is free → take it</text>
  <rect x="4" y="70" width="392" height="30" rx="5" stroke-width="1.5" style="fill: var(--viz-flow-soft); stroke: var(--viz-flow)" />
  <text x="14" y="91" font-size="16" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">2. below the max → open one (2–10 ms)</text>
  <rect x="4" y="108" width="392" height="30" rx="5" stroke-width="1.5" style="fill: var(--viz-warn-soft); stroke: var(--viz-warn)" />
  <text x="14" y="129" font-size="16" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">3. at the max → wait in line ≤ timeout</text>
  <text x="14" y="158" font-size="16" style="fill: var(--viz-bad)">timeout runs out → error, not a hang</text>

  <path d="M4 174 L396 174" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 4" style="stroke: var(--viz-stroke)" />
  <text x="4" y="198" font-size="18" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">one connection's life</text>

  <rect x="20" y="214" width="110" height="40" rx="8" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-surface); stroke: var(--viz-server)" />
  <text x="75" y="240" font-size="17" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">idle</text>
  <rect x="270" y="214" width="110" height="40" rx="8" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-flow-soft); stroke: var(--viz-flow)" />
  <text x="325" y="240" font-size="17" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">in use</text>
  <rect x="145" y="282" width="110" height="40" rx="8" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-bad-soft); stroke: var(--viz-bad)" />
  <text x="200" y="308" font-size="17" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">closed</text>

  <path d="M130 222 L268 222" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#cp-lc-a)" style="stroke: var(--viz-muted)" />
  <text x="200" y="215" font-size="15" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">acquire</text>
  <path d="M270 248 L132 248" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#cp-lc-a)" style="stroke: var(--viz-muted)" />
  <text x="200" y="267" font-size="15" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">release + reset</text>
  <path d="M60 254 L60 300 L143 300" fill="none" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#cp-lc-a)" style="stroke: var(--viz-bad)" />
  <text x="4" y="324" font-size="14" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">too old, idle, broken</text>
  <path d="M340 254 L340 300 L257 300" fill="none" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#cp-lc-a)" style="stroke: var(--viz-bad)" />
  <text x="396" y="324" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">broke in use</text>
</svg>
